hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"195","From Abu Hashem Ziyad bin Ayyub, from Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Humaid bin Abi Ghaniya, from my father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymira, on the authority of Shurayh ibn Hani, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted us permission for three days for the traveler, and one day... And a night for the present” meaning: in wiping over the socks."
